        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "showReserve"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SHOWRESERVE",
          "id": "1765818816564",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765818816567_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "a. Input Data: {{$context.$nodes.MERGERESERVEINVENTORY.$output.result}}\nb. Total LPN Count: {{$context.$nodes.MERGERESERVEINVENTORY.$output.total_lpn_count}}\n\nUse input \"{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\" to understand what the user wants.\n\nWhen the user asks about listing LPNs with expired inventory or inventory about to expire, follow these rules exactly:\n\n1. If Total LPN Count is 0 for an inbound request:\n   Output only:\n   Answer: There are no Inbound LPNs with the expired inventory.\n   Do not list anything else. TERMINATE here.\n\n2. If Total LPN Count is a non-zero integer:\n   - Show the total number of LPNs exactly as provided in Total LPN Count.\n   - Display only the first 20 LPNs, sorted by earliest expiry.\n   - Do not show the calculation used to reach the total.\n   - Render the results in a clean HTML table.\n\nOutput format:\n\nAnswer: There are <Total LPN Count> LPNs with the expired inventory.\nHere are the first few by earliest expiry listed below:\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Container Number</th>\n      <th>Item/SKU</th>\n      <th>Expiry Date</th>\n      <th>Location</th>\n      <th>Lock</th>\n      <th>Task Nbr</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>{LPN}</td>\n      <td>{Item}</td>\n      <td>{Expiry}</td>\n      <td>{Location}</td>\n      <td>{Container Lock}</td>\n      <td>{Task Nbr}</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\nRepeat one <tr> row for each LPN, up to a maximum of 20 rows.\n\nAfter displaying the expired inventory, ask the user:\n\n<strong>I can also help you by locking the Container or holding the tasks associated with the allocated LPNs.</strong><br>\n<strong>You can request this by saying:</strong><br>\n- Lock container {container_number} using lock code {lock_code}<br>\n- Hold the tasks ({task_Nbr})\n\nStrict formatting rules:\n- Always use an HTML table for the results.\n- Never merge multiple LPNs into one row.\n- Never place multiple records on the same line.\n- Never show more than 20 rows.\n- Never add extra commentary.\n- Never include calculations.\n- Preserve the field names exactly as written."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "showActive"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SHOWACTIVE",
          "id": "1765818858121",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765818858123_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Instructions:\n\na. Input Data:\n{{$context.$nodes.GETACTIVEEXPIREDINVENTORY.$output}}\n\nb. Use input:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nto understand the user’s request.\n\n?? Core Rules\n\nWhen the user asks about listing active locations with expired inventory or inventory about to expire, follow these rules exactly:\n\n1. Total Count Handling (CRITICAL)\nThe total number of locations is provided in: result_count\nYou must use result_count as the total value\nDo NOT calculate or infer the total from the number of rows displayed\nDo NOT assume the total equals the number of rows shown\n2. If Total Count = 0\n\nOutput only:\n\nAnswer: There are no Locations with the expired inventory.\nDo not add anything else\nDo not render a table\nTERMINATE immediately\n3. If Total Count > 0\n\nYou MUST:\n\nUse result_count as <n>\nSort results by Expiry (ascending – earliest first)\nDisplay only the first 20 records from the sorted results\nDo not display more than 20 rows under any circumstance\n?? Output Format (STRICT)\nAnswer: There are <n> Locations with the expired inventory.\nHere are the first few by earliest expiry listed below:\n\nThen render:\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Location</th>\n      <th>Item/SKU</th>\n      <th>Expiry Date</th>\n      <th>Task Nbr</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>{Location}</td>\n      <td>{Item}</td>\n      <td>{Expiry}</td>\n      <td>{Task Nbr}</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\nRepeat one <tr> per record\nMaximum: 20 rows only\n?? Mandatory Footer\n\nAfter the table, ALWAYS add:\n\n<strong>Note: Currently, locking of Active Inventory (or locations) is not supported.</strong><br>\n<strong>But I can help you with holding the tasks associated with the allocated inventory.</strong><br>\n<strong>You can request this by saying:</strong><br>\n- Hold the tasks {task_Nbr}\n?? Strict Rules (DO NOT VIOLATE)\n❌ Never use the number of displayed rows as the total\n❌ Never show more than 20 rows\n❌ Never merge multiple records into one row\n❌ Never place multiple records on the same line\n❌ Never include calculations or explanations\n❌ Never add extra commentary outside the defined format\n❌ Never change field names\n❌ Never skip sorting by earliest expiry"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "showOutbound"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SHOWOUTBOUND",
          "id": "1765818920177",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765818920179_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Instructions:\n\na. Input Data: {{$context.$nodes.GETOBEXPIREDINVENTORY.$output}}\n\nb. Use input \"{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\" to understand what the user wants.\n\nWhen the user asks about listing LPNs with expired inventory or inventory about to expire, follow these rules exactly:\n\n1. If the total number of LPNs is 0 for an outbound request:\n   Output only:\n   Answer: There are no Outbound LPNs with the expired inventory.\n   Do not list anything else. TERMINATE here.\n\n2. If the total number of LPNs is a non-zero integer:\n   - Show the total number of LPNs.\n   - Display only the first 20 LPNs, sorted by earliest expiry.\n   - Do not show the calculation used to reach the total.\n   - Render the results in a clean HTML table.\n\nOutput format:\n\nAnswer: There are <n> LPNs with the expired inventory.\nHere are the first few by earliest expiry listed below:\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Container Number</th>\n      <th>Item/SKU</th>\n      <th>Expiry Date</th>\n      <th>Location</th>\n      <th>Lock</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>{LPN}</td>\n      <td>{Item}</td>\n      <td>{Expiry}</td>\n      <td>{Location}</td>\n      <td>{Container Lock}</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\nRepeat one <tr> row for each LPN, up to a maximum of 20 rows.\n\nAfter displaying the expired inventory, ask the user:\n\n<strong>I can also help you with cancelling or locking the container.</strong><br>\n<strong>You can request this by saying:</strong><br>\n- Lock container {container_number} using lock code {lock_code}<br>\n- Cancel the containers {container_nbr}\n\nStrict formatting rules:\n- Always use an HTML table for the results.\n- Never merge multiple LPNs into one row.\n- Never place multiple records on the same line.\n- Never show more than 20 rows.\n- Never add extra commentary.\n- Never include calculations.\n- Preserve the field names exactly as written."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1766091655893",
            "name": "deriveContainer"
