              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an information extraction and validation assistant.\n\nInput message:\n\"{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\"\n\n\n\nTask:\nDerive:\n\ncontainer_nbr: array of container identifiers from the input (or null)\nreason_code: reason code from the input (or null)\nExtraction rules:\n\nIdentify the phrase \"with reason code\" (case-insensitive). If not present, set both fields to null and stop.\nExtract reason_code as the text after \"with reason code\" up to end of string; trim whitespace. If empty, set reason_code to null.\nEverything BEFORE the phrase \"with reason code\" is the container section.\nIn the container section, remove any leading command words like \"cancel\", \"cance\", \"cancel container\", \":\" or \"-\" (case-insensitive). Do not require exact spelling; treat \"cance\" as \"cancel\".\nThe remaining text is <containers>. Split by comma into a list, trim whitespace, and remove empty entries.\nDo not infer/approximate container IDs beyond splitting/trim. If no containers remain after cleanup, set container_nbr to null.\nOutput:\nReturn ONLY valid JSON:\n{\n\"container_nbr\": <array of strings OR null>,\n\"reason_code\": <string OR null>\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{ \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"container_nbr\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"reason_code\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"ContainerID\": { \"type\": \"integer\" } } }",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
