              "id": "1774920084476_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Instructions:\n\na. Input Data: {{$context.$nodes.MERGERESERVEALLOCATED.$output.result}}\n\nb. Use input \"{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\" to understand what the user wants.\n\nWhen the user asks about listing Allocated LPNs with expired inventory or inventory about to expire, follow these rules exactly:\n\n1. If the total number of LPNs is 0 for an inbound request:\n   Output only:\n   Answer: There are no allocated Inbound LPNs with the expired inventory.\n   Do not list anything else. TERMINATE here.\n\n2. If the total number of LPNs is a non-zero integer:\n   - Show the total number of LPNs.\n   - Display only the first 20 LPNs, sorted by earliest expiry.\n   - Do not show the calculation used to reach the total.\n   - Render the results in a clean HTML table.\n\nOutput format:\n\nAnswer: There are <n> expired LPNs with tasks.\nHere are the first few by earliest expiry listed below:\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Container Number</th>\n      <th>Item/SKU</th>\n      <th>Expiry Date</th>\n      <th>Location</th>\n      <th>Lock</th>\n      <th>Task Nbr</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>{LPN}</td>\n      <td>{Item}</td>\n      <td>{Expiry}</td>\n      <td>{Location}</td>\n      <td>{Container Lock}</td>\n      <td>{Task Nbr}</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\nRepeat one <tr> row for each LPN, up to a maximum of 20 rows.\n\nAfter displaying the expired inventory, ask the user:\n\n<strong>I can also help you with holding the tasks associated with the allocated LPNs.</strong><br>\n<strong>You can request this by saying:</strong><br>\n- Hold the tasks ({task_Nbr})\n\nStrict formatting rules:\n- Always use an HTML table for the results.\n- Never merge multiple LPNs into one row.\n- Never place multiple records on the same line.\n- Never show more than 20 rows.\n- Never add extra commentary.\n- Never include calculations.\n- Preserve the field names exactly as written."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1774919441889",
            "name": "showActiveTask"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SHOWACTIVETASK",
          "id": "1774920442439",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774920442442_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Instructions:\n\na. Input Data: {{$context.$nodes.GETTASKFOREXPIREDACTIVEINVENTORY.$output}}\n\nb. Use input \"{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\" to understand what the user wants.\n\nWhen the user asks about listing active locations with allocated expired inventory or inventory about to expire, follow these rules exactly:\n\n1. If the total number of active locations is 0:\n   Output only:\n   Answer: There are no Locations with the allocated expired inventory.\n   Do not list anything else. TERMINATE here.\n\n2. If the total number of active locations is a non-zero integer:\n   - Show the total number of locations.\n   - Display only the first 20 locations, sorted by earliest expiry.\n   - Do not show the calculation used to reach the total.\n   - Render the results in a clean HTML table.\n\nOutput format:\n\nAnswer: There are <n> Locations with the allocated expired inventory.\nHere are the first few by earliest expiry listed below:\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Location</th>\n      <th>Item/SKU</th>\n      <th>Expiry Date</th>\n      <th>Task Nbr</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>{Location}</td>\n      <td>{Item}</td>\n      <td>{Expiry}</td>\n      <td>{Task Nbr}</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\nRepeat one <tr> row for each location, up to a maximum of 20 rows.\n\nAfter displaying the expired inventory, add:\n\n<strong>Note: Currently, locking of Active Inventory (or locations) is not supported.</strong><br>\n<strong>But I can help you with holding the tasks associated with the allocated inventory.</strong><br>\n<strong>You can request this by saying:</strong><br>\n- Hold the tasks {task_Nbr}\n\nStrict formatting rules:\n- Always use an HTML table for the results.\n- Never merge multiple locations into one row.\n- Never place multiple records on the same line.\n- Never show more than 20 rows.\n- Never add extra commentary.\n- Never include calculations.\n- Preserve the field names exactly as written."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
