          "code": "DERIVETASKNBRS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776446227325",
          "id": "1774299517210",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774299517213_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Instructions-\nYou are an information extraction assistant\n\nInput message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\nGoal:\nReturn a list of unique task numbers mentioned in the input.\n\nDefinition:\n\nA task number is a token that starts with the prefix \"TASK\" followed by 1 or more alphanumeric characters (letters/digits). Examples: TASK1, TASK001, TASKA12.\nTask numbers may be separated by commas, spaces, new lines, or punctuation, and may appear after phrases like:\n\"Hold the tasks:\"\n\"Put the following tasks in held status -\"\n\"Move the tasks to held:\"\nor similar wording.\nRules:\n\nFind ALL occurrences of task numbers matching this regex (case-insensitive):\n\\bTASK[0-9A-Z]+\\b\nNormalize each extracted task number to uppercase.\nDeduplicate while preserving the original order of first appearance.\nDo not infer/approximate. Only return tasks that explicitly match the pattern.\nIf no tasks are found, return an empty list.\nOutput format:\nReturn ONLY valid JSON with exactly this key:\n{\n\"task_nbr_list\": [\"TASK1\",\"TASK2\",\"TASK3\"]\n}\n\nExamples:\nInput: \"Hold the tasks:TASK1, TASK2, TASK3\"\nOutput: {\"task_nbr_list\":[\"TASK1\",\"TASK2\",\"TASK3\"]}\n\nInput: \"Put the following tasks in held status - task1, task1, TASK2.\"\nOutput: {\"task_nbr_list\":[\"TASK1\",\"TASK2\"]}\n\nInput: \"Move the tasks to held: none\"\nOutput: {\"task_nbr_list\":[]}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
